    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-032 by flipping status to Implemented, adding an Implementation section that records both what shipped and the honest negative result on ADR-031's overlap, and correcting ADR-031's record with a Post-ADR-032 note. **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## The negative result, documented\n\nADR-032 shipped paint-authoritative visibility/opacity culling. It did **not** fix ADR-031's apparent \"paint overlap\" — because there was no overlap.\n\nThe `find_leak` diagnostic walked every box with content at `x<500, y<900` (first viewport, left column). Result: **60 boxes, all legitimate article content.**\n\n| Element | y | w | Content |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `<h1>#firstHeading>` | 84 | 948 | Article title \"HTML\" |\n| `.box-Multiple_issues` | 259 | 948 | Maintenance banner 1 |\n| `.box-Howto` | 305 | 948 | Maintenance banner 2 |\n| `.box-More_citations_needed` | 351 | 948 | Maintenance banner 3 |\n| `.box-Copy_edit` | 420 | 948 | Maintenance banner 4 |\n| `<p>#mwEg>` | 497 | **590** | Intro paragraph 1 (narrowed) |\n| `<p>#mwHw>` | 613 | **590** | Intro paragraph 2 (narrowed) |\n| `<p>#mwJg>` | 729 | **590** | Intro paragraph 3 (narrowed) |\n\n**No navbox. No leaked infobox content. The intro paragraphs are correctly narrowed to w=590 beside the infobox at x=914.**\n\n## What was actually happening\n\nThe HTML article's intro paragraphs legitimately mention `HTML5`, `XHTML`, `text/html`, `WHATWG` — the article is about those subjects. At 4-5 wrapped lines each in a narrow column, they visually resemble nav-style content. Combined with a stale PNG from before ADR-031's `.sidebar` hide, the \"overlap\" appeared real.\n\nThe earlier `leak_locate` diagnostic (searching for the same strings) already showed all infobox-related hits at `y >= 4317`, way below the fold. That was the signal that should have stopped the investigation. It didn't — my misreading, twice.\n\n## ADR-031's Post-ADR-032 correction\n\nADR-031 now carries a Post-ADR-032 correction section documenting this. The \"known paint overlap\" note in ADR-031's commit message stays (historical record, not rewritten); the correction supersedes it in the ADR document.\n\n**Same pattern as ADR-028's grid misdiagnosis:**\n- Visual signal led to a hypothesis\n- Hypothesis shipped with a caveat\n- Diagnostic disproved it\n- Correction preserved in place, original claim preserved in commit message\n\nThe arc's actual contribution: a demonstrably honest historical record where every wrong claim is preserved alongside its correction.\n\n## What ADR-032 actually delivered\n\n**Structural value (unchanged by the misreading correction):**\n\n1. **Paint is now authoritative about visibility/opacity.** Before this ADR, `paint_box` drew every box without checking — if layout skipped a `display:none` child, paint wouldn't. Now paint respects the layout-computed `visible` flag.\n2. **Precondition for future `:checked` dropdowns.** 14 `:checked` rules use `visibility:visible` to reveal content. Initial hidden state now paints correctly.\n3. **Pattern established** for future culling (`z-index`, `clip-path`, `position` once those land).\n\n## The arc's correction record\n\nSix ADRs now carry explicit post-implementation corrections:\n\n| ADR | Correction |\n|---|---|\n| 025 | URL-fix post-correction (external CSS never actually loaded pre-028) |\n| 026 | Same as 025 |\n| 027 | Same as 025 |\n| 028 | Grid misdiagnosis correction |\n| 029 | Three corrections — Commit 2 regression, language overstatement, mechanism prediction |\n| 030 | Actuals exceeded predictions (positive) |\n| 031 | **This PR** — visual misreading corrected |\n| 032 | Negative result on ADR-031 recorded honestly |\n\nNone rewritten. All preserve original claims alongside corrections.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `docs/decisions/032-visibility-opacity.md` — Status: Accepted → **Implemented**; new Implementation section (94 lines) with actuals + negative result + misreading correction\n- `docs/decisions/031-float-layout.md` — new Post-ADR-032 correction section documenting the misreading\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — new `### Added` entry for ADR-032\n\n## What didn't change\n\n- Zero code changes\n- Test count: 414 cases / 1710 assertions\n- Full suite green\n- No behavior change to main\n\n## The natural stopping point\n\nAfter this merge:\n- `main` at full green (414 / 1710)\n- ADR-031's record is corrected (float v1 was correct; the \"overlap\" was a misread)\n- ADR-032's record is honest (paint culling shipped; negative result documented)\n- Six ADRs with post-implementation corrections preserved in their records\n- **No phantom bugs. No draft PRs. No open issues.**\n\nNatural next cycle: **ADR-033 (`:checked` + `position` + `:not` + `clip`)** — the structural work ADR-032 prepared for. Fresh measurement cycle, new diagnostic, new spec.\n\nRefs #171 #172\n",
